WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.385
Every rule has a validation dataset,

2
00:00:02.385 --> 00:00:05.575
and a rule that can't be
shown to fire isn't finished.

3
00:00:05.575 --> 00:00:08.830
The known-bad half is an
event the rule must find,

4
00:00:08.830 --> 00:00:13.338
from the guide's synthetic events
or a replay on a ring zero device.

5
00:00:13.338 --> 00:00:17.022
The known-good half is a window
the rule must stay quiet in,

6
00:00:17.022 --> 00:00:18.825
or stay under its threshold.

7
00:00:18.825 --> 00:00:22.850
Then schema governance, the
program's risk-based recommendation.

8
00:00:22.850 --> 00:00:26.261
Each rule file names the
tables and columns it reads,

9
00:00:26.261 --> 00:00:31.338
and a weekly review runs each rule's query
and fails it when a column is renamed.

10
00:00:31.338 --> 00:00:36.037
Microsoft Learn keeps a list of naming
changes in the advanced hunting schema.

11
00:00:36.037 --> 00:00:37.888
One limit shapes all of this.

12
00:00:37.888 --> 00:00:43.425
Advanced hunting keeps thirty days, so a
validation window is at most thirty days.

13
00:00:43.425 --> 00:00:49.153
Learn's page for the run hunting query A
P I says it defaults to thirty days, and

14
00:00:49.153 --> 00:00:54.770
takes an I S O eighty-six oh one time span,
such as P thirty D, which the lab uses.
